{
  "manifest_version": 1,
  "pack_id": "toneking",
  "display_name": "Tone King Imperial MKII",
  "vendor": "Neural DSP",
  "file_header": "neural_dsp_toneking",
  "switch_encoding": "numeric",
  "audio_unit": {
    "type": "aumf",
    "subtype": "TKI2",
    "manufacturer": "NDSP",
    "note": "`scripts/audit_manifest.py --pack toneking` adaptively writes multiple observed and synthetic values through the record-state format. It maps 94 of 255 numeric preset keys to 94 of the 96 published controls; the other two published parameters are host-only Preset Previous/Next actions. Of the remaining numeric keys, 158 retain alternate state without moving a published control and `tempo` rejects every observed alternate."
  },
  "description": "Production pack for Tone King Imperial MKII presets, which store 8-byte binary doubles inside PARAM records. Its 94 control-bearing writable keys are mapped to published Audio Unit controls with verified kinds, display names, ranges, and selector tables where applicable. Recipes and tone guidance cover the two amp channels, pedals, cabinet section, EQ, modulation, delay, reverb, and gain staging.",
  "internal_state": "The 159 parameters marked `internal` are retained for inspection and lossless state round-trip but are read-only. Adaptive multi-value probing showed that 158 preserve alternate state without moving a published Audio Unit control; `tempo` rejects every observed alternate. Generated specs use the 94 mapped writable controls instead.",
